{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1509049-exalted-teach-that-i-should-cling-to-life-like-a-tick-what-has-the-game-teach-you-\ud83d\ude42","id":1509049,"title":"Exalted teach that I should cling to life like a tick. What has the game teach you? \ud83d\ude42","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-20T09:48:25-07:00","id":1509049,"title":"Exalted teach that I should cling to life like a tick. What has the game teach you? \ud83d\ude42","content":"<div align=\"center\"> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><img data-align=\"center\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/498704231407288320/1098546856746819614/IMG_7631.jpg?width=964&amp;height=615\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/498704231407288320/1098546856746819614/IMG_7631.jpg?width=964&amp;height=615\" data-thumb-url=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/498704231407288320/1098546856746819614/IMG_7631.jpg?width=964&amp;height=615\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div><br /> </div> <div align=\"center\"> <hr /></div> It's super obvious that Exalted hates and despites resurrection in all its forms with all those &quot;You can <b>NOT </b>revive people&quot; restrictions everywhere, so it seems that there is a theme of trying to cling to something that it's lost is a bad thing and it's better to let go, or else you gonna create a sexy Adam-like husband when trying to revive someone (how is that a bad thing again????).<br /> <br /> But what about Immortality though? Since the same theme of &quot;Letting Go or You Gonna Stink Up the Place&quot; in resurrection stories usually also appears in stories about the follies of people who tries to live pasts their Expiration Date\u200b or when they try to preserve someone (or <i>something</i>) that should have been dead\u200b, and writers usually seems to communicate that this is a bad idea by making the preserving action actively worsen the world in some ways or the person do get to live forever, but their existence is a hellish one i.e <i>Eternal life</i> brings <i>eternal pain</i>\u200b and stuff like that.<br /> <br /> Yet there doesn't seem to have any such distaste for immortality in Exalted unlike Resurrection though aside from one sentence in the Working section requires the resurrection method to not just simply be &quot;You get to live forever!&quot;, and people who live a long time in Exalted doesn't turn into fish people or contributing to rotten the metaphysics of Creation so is the theme of Letting Go only apply to Ressurection?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T11:04:30-07:00","id":1509067,"title":"","content":"&quot;Immortality is a bummer, I mean really&quot; is a line that Mnemon would tell people to discourage people from getting on her own footing... just like mommy did! It's a lot like the &quot;heavy is the head that wears the crown&quot; trope - kings certainly don't want other people to think that they could be king, and so make a production out of responsibilities and duties when the truth is that they run things and don't like upstarts.<br /> <br /> Tangentially related, the picture on the left makes me think &quot;Mnemon Versus the Forces of Anathema&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T14:47:42-07:00","id":1509103,"title":"","content":"The reason it has no distaste for immortality is because it isn't playing a &quot;Letting Go&quot; theme with the no resurrection thing. It's playing a &quot;Measure Twice, Cut Once&quot; theme. Same with the no time travel and (in 3rd) the lack of any way to cleanly undo a sorcerous working.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":572,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","user":"Verzio","date":". 04-21-2023, 02:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T12:27:41-07:00","id":1509225,"title":"","content":"Aww, I was hoping this was gonna be a thread about how the game affected people's real life world view.<br /> <br /> The necessity of moving on doesn't seem to be an active theme behind the fact of no resurrection, but it's probably a necessary adaptation inherent to the fact that some things a person cares about will inevitably die and cannot be brought back.<br /> <br /> Although perhaps some extent of needing to be at peace with mortality is a bit ingrained in the game. Maiden of Endings and all.<br /> <br /> I think the immortality with complications thing is primarily concerned with creating interesting drama more than making some broad comment on the basic concept. Really, I've long felt as though arguments in fiction about immortality are kind of pointless unless they're part of some abstract or analogous reflection, because like... there's no effectual advocacy for immortality.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1509049-exalted-teach-that-i-should-cling-to-life-like-a-tick-what-has-the-game-teach-you-\ud83d\ude42?p=1509067#post1509067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Tangentially related, the picture on the left makes me think &quot;Mnemon Versus the Forces of Anathema&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's Steven Universe font.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T18:40:35-07:00","id":1509245,"title":"","content":"Death by aging doesn't come up &quot;on stage&quot; in rpg's that often. Even in Ars Magica games that run decades and use ageing rules that can kill characters I don't see it that often.<br /> <br /> Therefore, death by ageing is not a common source of drama in games. Immortality in Exalted is bundled with consequences in attempt to make sure it adds drama. On the other hand, death by getting yourself killed is a frequent source of drama in games. Resurrection very often removes drama.<br /> <br /> That's my take anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-22T06:23:39-07:00","id":1509270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1509049-exalted-teach-that-i-should-cling-to-life-like-a-tick-what-has-the-game-teach-you-\ud83d\ude42?p=1509225#post1509225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's Steven Universe font.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wasn't really thinking about the font, there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-22T12:49:56-07:00","id":1509306,"title":"","content":"I'd also say death by aging doesn't come up because players generally set their character age, so unless the player wants to deal with their character being concerned about the fact that they've hit the point where death is now a likely outcome of going to sleep with no external factors takes some of the drama out of it. That and even if you are playing a character with that condition you're unlikely to have your DM/ST/SG/GM/HG to be rolling whenever your character goes to sleep to see if your character dies in the middle of the night as that would be unsatisfying. <br /> <br /> As for thematics they kind of say it in the book, the reason resurrection is ,canonically, off limits is the same reason time travel is off limits. No undoing mistakes. Like there's a certain level of ease and insanity that comes in some games when your characters are aware that death is something of a temporary state which can be undone with effects comparable to a particularly bad hangover. I also suspect its to handle a few confusing questions.<br /> Like if your e3 dawn dies and gets raised, what's the time table on them not getting their exaltation back because its now empowering someone else? Does it automatically return to a returned bearer/host if it doesn't have a new one? What happens if we raise multiple prior hosts of the exaltation at the same gap? Hell how much of an exalts powers do they get to keep if they don't have an exaltation anymore? Its just way easier to go, &quot;Trying to bring back the dead doesn't work. Occaisionally you get super zombies, but they're their own thing. Also I guess trying to raise said super zombie that's been perma killed can also result in super zombie.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T08:27:27-07:00","id":1509586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1509049-exalted-teach-that-i-should-cling-to-life-like-a-tick-what-has-the-game-teach-you-\ud83d\ude42?p=1509067#post1509067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Immortality is a bummer, I mean really&quot; is a line that Mnemon would tell people to discourage people from getting on her own footing... just like mommy did! It's a lot like the &quot;heavy is the head that wears the crown&quot; trope - kings certainly don't want other people to think that they could be king, and so make a production out of responsibilities and duties when the truth is that they run things and don't like upstarts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, kinda like those newspaper strips that I sometimes saw long ago where they go &quot;Being rich is actually not that good since you will become so lonely uwu&quot;.<br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1509049-exalted-teach-that-i-should-cling-to-life-like-a-tick-what-has-the-game-teach-you-\ud83d\ude42?p=1509225#post1509225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aww, I was hoping this was gonna be a thread about how the game affected people's real life world view.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> Ah I was just seeing some Sekiro and then thought about how people who live for a long time in Exalted seem to have no trouble at all and decide to make this thread.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1509049-exalted-teach-that-i-should-cling-to-life-like-a-tick-what-has-the-game-teach-you-\ud83d\ude42?p=1509225#post1509225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Although perhaps some extent of needing to be at peace with mortality is a bit ingrained in the game. Maiden of Endings and all.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> Yeah, death gods looking for people who have lived past their appointed time is quite a common story hook for them so maybe the Sidereal book will have some pondering about Immortality in it, though I can't remember if gods even have a &quot;You will die on dd/mm/yy&quot; shackle slapped on or is that just a thing for human.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Apromor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1509049-exalted-teach-that-i-should-cling-to-life-like-a-tick-what-has-the-game-teach-you-\ud83d\ude42?p=1509245#post1509245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Death by aging doesn't come up &quot;on stage&quot; in rpg's that often. Even in Ars Magica games that run decades and use ageing rules that can kill characters I don't see it that often.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1509049-exalted-teach-that-i-should-cling-to-life-like-a-tick-what-has-the-game-teach-you-\ud83d\ude42?p=1509306#post1509306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd also say death by aging doesn't come up because players generally set their character age, so unless the player wants to deal with their character being concerned about the fact that they've hit the point where death is now a likely outcome of going to sleep with no external factors takes some of the drama out of it. That and even if you are playing a character with that condition you're unlikely to have your DM/ST/SG/GM/HG to be rolling whenever your character goes to sleep to see if your character dies in the middle of the night as that would be unsatisfying.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> Yeah games rarely last for hundreds of years for the PCs to grow old, but you can express the whole Immortality Suck with so many immortal-wannabe NPCs running around, like maybe include a story about a monarch whose pursuit of immortality curse her island forever and turns everyone there into fish people for example ~<br /> \u200b\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T17:15:58-07:00","id":1509649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1509049-exalted-teach-that-i-should-cling-to-life-like-a-tick-what-has-the-game-teach-you-\ud83d\ude42?p=1509586#post1509586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bAh I was just seeing some Sekiro and then thought about how people who live for a long time in Exalted seem to have no trouble at all and decide to make this thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ohhh, don't get me started on Sekiro. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> In any case, Exalted does not quite originate from the same philosophical foundation of the value of transient beauty.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, death gods looking for people who have lived past their appointed time is quite a common story hook for them so maybe the Sidereal book will have some pondering about Immortality in it, though I can't remember if gods even have a &quot;You will die on dd/mm/yy&quot; shackle slapped on or is that just a thing for human.<br /> \u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Not so much. It's really more an implication of the sutras of Saturn, the insistence that there's always an ending. There are gods who are genuinely immortal (if not unkillable) but on a long enough timeline, well, who can say, and it's hard not to ensure that the timeline after you will ultimately be so long as to make your great lifespan a footnote.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T13:01:36-07:00","id":1510241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1509049-exalted-teach-that-i-should-cling-to-life-like-a-tick-what-has-the-game-teach-you-\ud83d\ude42?p=1509649#post1509649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ohhh, don't get me started on Sekiro. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> In any case, Exalted does not quite originate from the same philosophical foundation of the value of transient beauty.<br /> <br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Living for a long time actively making the world a worse place is probably not too good a premise for something like ttrpg yeah\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}